      "text": "Developers use ODT to turn a requirement into clear scope, impacted files, hardened prompts, code guidance, unit-test guidance, and accessibility checkpoints.\n\nReviewers and tech leads use ODT to inspect evidence, add reviewer notes or stage overrides, request re-analysis, and standardize the software development process.\n\nPrimary interface: ODT/FEDIT dashboard with generated reports/odt artifacts for intake, impact, design, code, test, and compliance stages, delegation and action buttons.\n\nDay-to-day workflow: enter work item -> review generated evidence -> refine if needed -> delegate approved execution path -> review diffs -> approve or refine.\n\nValue realized: less repetitive planning effort, clearer scope, AI assisted coding and unit testing, more consistent review, earlier accessibility visibility, and better human + AI collaboration and accelerated delivery.\n",
